            <ArticleTitle>Contact with farming environment as a major risk factor for Shiga toxin (Vero cytotoxin)-producing Escherichia coli O157 infection in humans.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1049-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a prospective, unmatched case-control study of sporadic Shiga toxin (Vero cytotoxin)-producing Escherichia coli O157 (STEC O157) infection in England, exposure to the farming environment emerged strongly as a risk factor (adjusted odds ratio = 2.45; 95% confidence intervals = 1.49-4.02; p=0.0004) posing further challenges and opportunities for prevention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
